# Bun Runtime Rules (v1.3+ - 2025)

## What is Bun

Bun is an all-in-one toolkit for JavaScript and TypeScript apps that ships as a single executable, featuring a blazing-fast runtime, package manager, test runner, and bundler.

### Key Features
- **Fast Runtime**: Drop-in replacement for Node.js, built with Zig and JavaScriptCore
- **Package Manager**: 7× faster than npm, ~4× faster than pnpm
- **Test Runner**: Built-in test runner with Jest-compatible API
- **Bundler**: Native bundler for production builds
- **TypeScript Native**: Run TypeScript files directly, no compilation needed
- **Web Standard APIs**: Fetch, WebSocket, ReadableStream, and more
- **Built-in APIs**: Bun.serve, Bun.file, Bun.write, Bun.SQL

## Installation & Setup

### Install Bun
```bash
# macOS, Linux, WSL
curl -fsSL https://bun.sh/install | bash

# Windows
powershell -c "irm bun.sh/install.ps1|iex"

# Upgrade Bun
bun upgrade

# Check version
bun --version
```

### Initialize Project
```bash
# Create new project
bun init

# Install dependencies
bun install

# Run file
bun run index.ts
```

## Package Manager (7× Faster)

### Installation Commands
```bash
# Install all dependencies
bun install

# Install specific package
bun add react
bun add -d typescript
bun add -D @types/react

# Install exact version
bun add react@18.2.0

# Global install
bun add -g typescript

# Remove package
bun remove react

# Update packages
bun update

# Interactive update (v1.2+)
bun update --interactive
```

### Workspaces
```json
// package.json
{
  "name": "my-monorepo",
  "workspaces": ["packages/*", "apps/*"],
  "dependencies": {
    "react": "^19.0.0"
  }
}
```

```bash
# Install all workspace dependencies in one pass
bun install

# Run command in workspace
bun --filter my-app dev
bun --filter @org/package build
```

### bun.lockb
```bash
# Bun uses binary lockfile for faster parsing
# Convert to text-based (v1.2+)
bun install --yarn

# Use text-based bun.lock (default in v1.2+)
# Automatically generated on bun install
```

## Runtime Features

### Run TypeScript Directly
```typescript
// index.ts - No compilation needed!
import { serve } from 'bun'

const server = serve({
  port: 3000,
  fetch(req) {
    return new Response('Hello from Bun!')
  },
})

console.log(`Listening on http://localhost:${server.port}`)
```

```bash
# Run directly
bun run index.ts
# or just
bun index.ts
```

